/`0x9F`/`0xA0`/`0xBF` and the\n  out-of-continuation values, plus `'\\0'` (truncation)\n* truncation depth: sequence cut after 1 / 2 / 3 bytes by the NUL terminator\n* position of the first invalid byte: offset 0 (⇒ `memcpy` length 0) vs > 0\n  (⇒ prefix `memcpy`) vs none (⇒ `strdup` early-return path)\n* length / count: `\"\"` (0 bytes), 1 byte, \"few\", and counts that cross the\n  `repl < 3` / `REPLACEMENT_INC = 4096` accounting boundary\n  (1 / 1365 / 1366 / 1367 / 2730 / 2731 / 2732 / 4096 invalid bytes)\n* bytes after the terminating NUL (must be ignored)\n\n## Configuration table (cross-product, pruned to what the C distinguishes)\n\nEvery row is exercised against **both** `.so`s with **many randomized inputs**\n(seeded xorshift64\\*, fixed seed per row ⇒ reproducible) *and* the listed\nhand-derived boundary values. Test names refer to `tests/differential.rs`.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|----|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1  | `w_utf8_drop` | `\"\"` (empty) | [ ] |\n| 2  | `w_utf8_drop` | pure ASCII `0x01..0x7F`, exhaustive single bytes + random lengths 1..64 | [ ] |\n| 3  | `w_utf8_drop` | exhaustive **all 256** single-byte strings | [ ] |\n| 4  | `w_utf8_drop` | exhaustive **all 65536** two-byte strings | [ ] |\n| 5  | `w_utf8_drop` | exhaustive 3-byte strings over lead `0xE0..0xEF` × all 256 × all 256 | [ ] |\n| 6  | `w_utf8_drop` | exhaustive 4-byte strings over lead `0xF0..0xF7` × all 256 × sampled 3rd/4th | [ ] |\n| 7  | `w_utf8_drop` | well-formed 2-byte only (`0xC2..0xDF` + `0x80..0xBF`), random multi-char | [ ] |\n| 8  | `w_utf8_drop` | well-formed 3-byte only, incl. boundary `E0 A0 80`, `ED 9F BF`, `EE 80 80`, `EF BF BF` | [ ] |\n| 9  | `w_utf8_drop` | well-formed 4-byte only, incl. boundary `F0 90 80 80`, `F4 8F BF BF` | [ ] |\n| 10 | `w_utf8_drop` | mixed well-formed 1/2/3/4-byte, random lengths 0..256 | [ ] |\n| 11 | `w_utf8_drop` | uniformly random bytes,