{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BN4RhhdS4WpjQR2gt9bHhq","type":"tool_result","content":"=== only change to src/lib.rs vs. the original translation ===\n--- /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SBp7Tv/tmp/lib.rs.orig\t2026-08-20 17:18:21.853733105 +0000\n+++ src/lib.rs\t2026-08-20 17:39:48.247285564 +0000\n@@ -35,6 +35,14 @@\n /// `#define REPLACEMENT_INC 4096`\n const REPLACEMENT_INC: usize = 4096;\n \n+/// `__FILE__` as the C compiler sees it.\n+///\n+/// CMake compiles `c_src/src/lib.c` with an absolute path, so glibc's\n+/// `__assert_fail` prints the absolute path of that file.  Deriving the same\n+/// string from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` makes the abort message that reaches stderr\n+/// byte-identical to the C library's when both are built from one checkout.\n+const C_FILE: &[u8] = concat!(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"), \"/c_src/src/lib.c\\0\").as_bytes();\n+\n /// Reproduces `assert(string != NULL);` (the C library is compiled without\n /// `NDEBUG`, so the assertion is live and aborts the process).\n #[cold]\n@@ -43,7 +51,7 @@\n     unsafe {\n         __assert_fail(\n             b\"string != NULL\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n-            b\"src/lib.c\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n+            C_FILE.as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n             line,\n             function.as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n         )\n\n=== c_src contents (only build/ added) ===\nc_src\nc_src/CMakeLists.txt\nc_src/build\nc_src/include\nc_src/include/lib.h\nc_src/src\nc_src/src/lib.c","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07e979d6-63d7-48dc-ac71-77490c70e46a","uuid":"7fef6df8-85f3-48ff-a962-af3db26f55f4","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:42:10.026Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== only change to src/lib.rs vs. the original translation ===\n--- /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-SBp7Tv/tmp/lib.rs.orig\t2026-08-20 17:18:21.853733105 +0000\n+++ src/lib.rs\t2026-08-20 17:39:48.247285564 +0000\n@@ -35,6 +35,14 @@\n /// `#define REPLACEMENT_INC 4096`\n const REPLACEMENT_INC: usize = 4096;\n \n+/// `__FILE__` as the C compiler sees it.\n+///\n+/// CMake compiles `c_src/src/lib.c` with an absolute path, so glibc's\n+/// `__assert_fail` prints the absolute path of that file.  Deriving the same\n+/// string from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` makes the abort message that reaches stderr\n+/// byte-identical to the C library's when both are built from one checkout.\n+const C_FILE: &[u8] = concat!(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"), \"/c_src/src/lib.c\\0\").as_bytes();\n+\n /// Reproduces `assert(string != NULL);` (the C library is compiled without\n /// `NDEBUG`, so the assertion is live and aborts the process).\n #[cold]\n@@ -43,7 +51,7 @@\n     unsafe {\n         __assert_fail(\n             b\"string != NULL\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n-            b\"src/lib.c\\0\".as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n+            C_FILE.as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n             line,\n             function.as_ptr() as *const c_char,\n         )\n\n=== c_src contents (only build/ added) ===\nc_src\nc_src/CMakeLists.txt\nc_src/build\nc_src/include\nc_src/include/lib.h\nc_src/src\nc_src/src/lib.c","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kvfng7bxyrhnkt3jr2ycqlpq5eiawujaxqilmxhrvclqhfr5yfaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\n**1. The test harness was silently vacuous (the most important finding).**\n`cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` library — the integration tests don't reach it through the crate graph, so Cargo leaves a stale `target/debug/libdriver.so` in place. My first suite passed 46/46 tests against a `.so` built 15 minutes earlier. I only caught this because I ran a mutation check, which reported **0/12 injected bugs caught**. Fix: `tests/common/mod.rs::rust_so_path()` now shells out to `cargo build --lib` with a separate `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` and loads that `.so`. (Adding `\"rlib\"` to `crate-type` does *not* work — Cargo only builds `cdylib` for `cargo build`, never as a dependency edge.)\n\n**2. One real translation divergence:** the `assert()` abort message. C's `__FILE__` is the absolute path CMake passes; the Rust hardcoded `\"src/lib.c\"`, so stderr differed byte-for-byte. Now derived from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR + \"/c_src/src/lib.c\"`. This is the only change to `src/lib.rs` — the C logic itself was translated faithfully (verified bug-for-bug, including the signed-`char` `>= (char)0xC2` compare, the dead `0xEF` clause, and the `size_t repl` accounting).\n\n**3. Two measurement problems I had to solve properly rather than paper over:**\n- `RLIMIT_AS` alone cannot force `malloc` failure in a forked child — the child inherits the parent's heap free space. Replaced with `exhaust_allocator()` (clamp the limit, then drain the allocator with a descending size ladder). For the `realloc` row, reserving exactly `strlen+1` bytes before draining makes the first `malloc` succeed and the first `realloc` fail — with a `replacement=0` control that must *succeed*, proving the realloc branch (not the malloc branch) was hit.\n- `malloc_usable_size` compared in-process is meaningless (allocator state differs between the two calls). The two children are now forked **back-to-back** from a bit-identical heap, which makes `size = strlen+1 + g·REPLACEMENT_INC` exactly comparable. This is what catches allocation-schedule bugs that produce identical output bytes.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — symbol diff is **empty**; both `w_utf8_drop` and `w_utf8_filter` exported, no stubs, no untranslated C.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 28 rejection rows, all with passing differential tests.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 47 configuration rows, all passing across randomized inputs. Includes the low-level `w_utf8_drop` entry point directly, out-of-range `_Bool` values across FFI, and a `PROT_NONE` guard page proving neither implementation reads past the NUL.\n- `verify_all.sh` — 1 valid feature combination (`Cargo.toml` declares none; `c_src` has no build-time switches); `cargo check` + `nm -D` parity + full suite in **both** `dev` and `release` (release flips `panic = \"abort\"`).\n- `mutation_check.sh` — **19/19** injected bugs caught in both profiles.\n\nOne honest limitation: `REPLACEMENT_INC 4096 → 4095` is only caught via the fork-based allocation-size probe at large replacement counts (≥ ~16 realloc rounds); below that, glibc's 16-byte chunk granularity hides it, and it is unobservable through the public ABI. `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the `build/` directory the task instructed me to create."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1072,"cache_read_input_tokens":212433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1072,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07e979d6-63d7-48dc-ac71-77490c70e46a","uuid":"c793fd6e-5543-4b44-b44f-972703dc7c07","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:42:29.419Z"}
